# Context

## Why This Way
BenchmarkIngestAppend must ingest genuine inserts: every batch has to sit
above the source's committed cursor, or the write path treats it as an
idempotent replay (which BenchmarkIngestReplay already measures). The 16 MiB
corpus yields only ~470 eight-record windows, but the benchmark framework
owns b.N and grows it until benchtime is met — on fast storage (CI runners)
that passes the cap within the default 1 s. A benchmark over a bounded
stream therefore cannot b.Fatalf on exhaustion; it must re-prime.

The re-prime swaps in a fresh database file (close, remove db/-wal/-shm,
store.Open, RegisterSource, ingest the 1024-event prefix) with the benchmark
timer stopped, then wraps the window index. Alternatives rejected:
ingesting below the cursor measures replay, not append; a new source per lap
grows the database without bound as hardware gets faster; a bigger corpus
only moves the cap.

## Gotchas
- The prefix re-ingest cost is excluded via StopTimer/StartTimer; keep it
  that way or the append rows silently include setup.
- store.Close checkpoints and removes the WAL files on clean close, so the
  -wal/-shm removes are belt-and-braces for crash-leftovers.

